  "details": "Disabling and Re-enabling self-interact fixes this issue, but because I had to disable it from its enabled state, it isn't obvious that someone would have to do this.\nNot sure if this happens with avatars uploaded online.\nSteps I remember taking that lead me to this moment. I cannot reproduce this bug.\nOpened up my Avatar Dynamics unity project and added two Contact Recievers and two Contact Senders and added a list of collision tags. I updated my animation controller to set off sound effects when those tags were read. I adjusted the collision tags of another sender and receiver. I uploaded locally and then discovered this bug. Re-uploading failed to fix itself. Only when I disabled self-interact and then re-enabled it did everything work fine.",
